\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Contents - Maintenance
\par \pard \plain\fs24 User maintenance on this series of instruments is very limited, and is restricted to items that \ul do not\plain\fs24  require any panels to be removed in order to gain access to them.
\par 
\par \b\scaps there are no user serviceable parts behind the panels , and removal of a panel exposes high voltages and highly sensitive electronic circuitry.\plain\fs24 
\par User serviceable items are as follows:-
\par \uldb \b Firing Unit\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cleaning_the_Gun_Assembly}
\par \uldb Anode Cleaning\plain\b\fs24 {\v Anode_Cleaning}\plain\f3\fs24 
\par \uldb \f2\b Final \'91variabl{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Contents}
e\'92 Aperture replacement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cleaning_the_Aperture_Assembly}
\par \pard \plain\f3\fs24 
\par \f2\b 
\par \uldb Desiccator Silica Crystal replacement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Air_Admittance_Drier_Assembly}
\par \uldb Anode support \plain\b\fs24 {\v Dismantling_and_Cleaning_of_Anode_Support} and \uldb polepieces\plain\b\fs24 {\v H6.3KN}
\par \uldb Rotary pump oil changes\plain\b\fs24 {\v Rotary_Pump_Oil_Level}
\par ALL\plain\fs24  other maintenance operations, including these, if required, should be carried out by LEO Service Engineers, or authorised agents, and will be done on Service and Period Maintenance visits. These include:-
