{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Rotary Pump Oil Level}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Rotary_Pump_Oil_Level}
\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Rotary Pump Oil Level
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Check the oil level in the sight glass on the pump. 
\par The minimum oil level is the lower edge of the sight glass. 
\par The maximum level is 25mm below the top of the glass.  
\par When necessary top up with oil of the type specified for the particular pump in use (i.e. Edwards no 15 for Edwards pump, or Alcatel VP1 for Alcatel pumps).
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Air Admittance Drier Assembly}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Air_Admittance_Drier_Assembly}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Air Admittance Drier Assembly}
\b\fs32\cf1 Air Admittance Drier Assembly
\par \pard \plain\fs24 If the air drier is allowed to become ineffective the pump down time of the SEM will become longer than normal.  
\par The assembly is mounted on the rear panel of the plinth. 
\par The colour of the desiccant in the assembly should be checked daily and if it shows signs of becoming saturated, i.e. turning from pink to white, it should be replaced or reactivated.  If the pump down time is becoming longer than expected then the dessicant should be checked.The procedure below should be followed
\par \pard 
\par To renew the desiccant:-
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Unclip the drier from the rear of the plinth.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Unscrew the large knurled retaining ring from one end of the assembly and remove the end cap.  Remove the filter washer beneath it.  The desiccant can now be poured out and either dried or discarded.  Remove the remaining filter washer and the perforated metal support.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Clean the parts by washing in a suitable solvent, e.g. diluted liquid detergent, after which each part must be thoroughly rinsed and dried.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Replace the perforated metal support with the concave side facing away from where the desiccant will be.  Cover with two filter washers (shiny side away from the desiccant).  Fill the assembly with new or reactivated desiccant.  Fit a filter washer with the shiny side towards the desiccant.  Fit the end cap and knurled clamp ring.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Refit the assembly to the rear of the plinth.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab 
