{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Cleaning the Gun Assembly}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Cleaning_the_Gun_Assembly}
\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Cleaning the Gun Assembly
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Vent the column and chamber to air.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Open the gun.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Loosen the three filament assembly clamp screws (see \ul \b\ul Firing Unit\plain\b\fs24 {\v Firing_Unit}\plain\fs24 ) and remove the firing unit.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Lift out the anode (see \ul \b\ul Column\plain\b\fs24 {\v 19A.J.D}\plain\fs24 ). 
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Close the gun and pump the system while the components are cleaned. Take the filament assembly and anode to a clean area for cleaning.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Using the flat metal key unscrew the height adjustment ring and remove the filament carrier.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Loosen the four screws (see \ul \b\ul Firing Unit\plain\b\fs24 {\v Firing_Unit}\plain\fs24 ) holding the filament into the carrier and remove the filament.
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Using thumb pressure push out the gun aperture disk and its retaining clip from the grid cap.  Clean and inspect the gun aperture disk, if it is badly scratched or distorted replace it.  \uldb Clean the anode\plain\fs24 {\v Anode_Cleaning} and the filament carrier (if removed).
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab 
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Replace the anode into the anode support.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab If necessary change the filament, centre it in the grid and replace the assembly in the gun (as described in\i  \plain\fs24  \uldb \i\b Changing the Filament\plain\i\b\fs24 {\v 2MRA_.K@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24 ).
\par \f4 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f2 \tab Pump down the column and chamber and run up the gun, not forgetting to check the filament saturation and gun alignment, as these may have changed with the new filament.
\par \page
