{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Cleaning the Aperture Assembly}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Cleaning_the_Aperture_Assembly}
\pard\keepn \f2\b\fs32\cf1 Cleaning the Aperture Assembly
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 1.\tab Vent the column and chamber to air.
\par 2.\tab Remove the four screws holding the aperture changer into the column  and remove this assembly from the column.
\par 3.\tab Take the aperture assembly to a clean area for cleaning.
\par 4.\tab Remove the two screws holding the aperture clamp plate onto the aperture blade (see\ul \b\ul  Final Aperture Changer\plain\b\fs24 {\v VTLIYS}\plain\fs24 ).  Lift off the clamp plate and remove the apertures.  \b\cf2 The aperture blade must not\plain\b\fs24\cf2  be removed from its mounting arm.\plain\b\fs24  \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\cf2 5.\plain\fs24 \tab Clean the aperture clamp plate. The aperture blade should be carefully polished ensuring that the mounting arm does not become distorted.  The aperture blade can be cleaned by agitating it in a shallow beaker of solvent.\b\cf2 
\par \plain\fs24 6.\b\cf2 \tab \plain\fs24 Insert new apertures into the aperture blade and fit the aperture clamp plate and screws. Refit the aperture blade to the aperture changer. Ensure that the blade is horizontal, and is not tilted to the side.
\par 7.\tab Clean the 'O' ring on the aperture changer and replace the assembly into the column and secure with the four screws.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \f3\fs32\cf3 The apertures have one flat side, the other side being shaped like a funnel. The apertures must be mounted in the blade with the flat side upwards when the aperture changer is mounted in the column.\plain\f3\fs20 
