{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} B5GCZ0}
\pard \fs32\cf1 Column Dismantling
\par \plain\fs24 This is part of the\uldb  Basic Colummn Dismantling, Cleaning and Reassembly Procedure\plain\fs24 {\v Basic_Column_Dismantling__Cleaning_and_Reassembly}
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab Remove the anode from the anode support.  Undo the four screws securing the anode support and remove it vertically.
\par 2.\tab Insert the special tool (Pt No 719951) into the C\fs12 1\fs24  polepiece assembly and remove by lifting vertically.  Write down the serial number of this polepiece assembly.
\par 3.\tab Remove the C\fs12 2\fs24  polepiece assembly in the same manner also noting its serial number.  Lift off the wavy washer from the top of the C\fs12 2\fs24  polepiece assembly and store safely.  Replace the gun lid on the column and pump the system.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See\ul \b\ul  Column Diagram\plain\b\fs24 {\v 19A.J.D}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Dismantling and Cleaning of Anode Support}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Dismantling_and_Cleaning_of_Anode_Support}
\pard \b\fs32\cf1 Dismantling and Cleaning of Anode Support
\par \plain\fs24 This is part of the\uldb  Basic Colummn Dismantling, Cleaning and Reassembly Procedure\plain\fs24 {\v Basic_Column_Dismantling__Cleaning_and_Reassembly}
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab Place the low kV anode into the anode support and measure the Gap 'A' between the top of the anode support and the bottom of the anode (see \ul \b\ul Anode Support\plain\b\fs24 {\v Anode_Support}\plain\fs24 ).
\par 2.\tab Remove the two screws holding the spray aperture from the bottom of the anode support and extract the spray aperture.
\par \tab Loosen the liner securing screw and remove the liner tube from the anode support.  Carefully clean all of the components ensuring that all traces of contamination are removed.  After cleaning inspect the spray aperture using a low power magnifier.  Replace it if it is distorted or scratched near the orifice.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 3.\tab Reassemble the anode support, adjusting the liner tube position so that the Gap 'A', using the low kV anode, is the same as before.  Insert the spray aperture and secure with two screws.
\par \page
